  - id: the_form_of_a_servant
    displayName: The Form of a Servant
    flavorText: Christ, being in the form of God, empties himself and takes the form
      of a servant, humbling himself unto death on a cross, so that God highly exalts
      him and gives him the name above every name.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: The ultimate pattern for the unity and lowliness of mind Paul urges
      on the Philippians - Christ's own self-emptying, humbling, obedience unto death,
      and subsequent exaltation, presented as the model believers are called to imitate
      in how they treat one another.
